\description{
Calibrates a run's scores against a control set, for research: how far the scores separate its P controls from its B controls, and the functional classes thresholds make (abnormal-like, intermediate, WT-like: classes in this assay, never a classification of a variant). Returns the ROC curve's AUC with DeLong's interval, the precision-recall curve's area, both with a seeded stratified bootstrap's intervals; the thresholds, set by the controls (rule error: at most `error` of either side's controls in the other side's class; youden: one threshold of the largest sensitivity + specificity) or given (abnormal and normal); each side's controls and the run's variants in each class; sensitivity (P abnormal-like) and specificity (B WT-like) with Wilson's intervals; how far the bootstrap moves the thresholds; and the evidence strength each class would give, for research: its OddsPath as Brnich et al. 2019 define it (one control of the other side added) with the strength their Table 3 makes of it (PS3 for the abnormal-like class, BS3 for the WT-like), the bootstrap's interval and strengths with the thresholds kept, and what limits it (thresholds set on the same controls, few controls in a class, circularity). Kept with the workspace and shown in the Calibrate view; nothing calibrates by itself.
}
